## 31.7 Interactive Information Dashboard Design: reactable and reactablefmtr methods

In order to build interactive sparklines, the `dataui` R package (loaded at setup) is required as a backend for `reactablefmtr`.

### 31.7.1 Plotting interactive sparklines

Similar to gtExtras, to plot interactive sparklines using the `reactablefmtr` package we need to prepare the list field by using the code chunk below.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
report <- report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize(`Monthly Sales` = list(Sales))
```
:::


Next, `react_sparkline` will be used to plot the sparklines as shown below.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
reactable(
  report,
  columns = list(
    Product = colDef(maxWidth = 200),
    `Monthly Sales` = colDef(
      cell = react_sparkline(report)
    )
  )
)
```

